Name the Windows library that provides the futex functions the Rust standard library uses

deps/crates is compiled by cargo into node_crates.lib, and Node hands that archive to
the platform linker like any other static library. The Rust standard library waits on
an address with WaitOnAddress, WakeByAddressSingle and WakeByAddressAll - MSDN puts
those three in synchapi.h, provided by Synchronization.lib, served at run time by
API-MS-Win-Core-Synch-l1-2-0.dll - and nothing in Node's build asks the linker for
that library. So every link of node_crates.lib (mksnapshot.exe first, then node.exe
and libnode) ends with

    error LNK2019: unresolved external symbol __imp_WaitOnAddress
    error LNK2019: unresolved external symbol __imp_WakeByAddressSingle
    error LNK2019: unresolved external symbol __imp_WakeByAddressAll
        referenced in file node_crates.lib(std-*.rcgu.o)

Whether you see it depends on the Rust version, which is why a Node version that built
last week can fail this week with no change of its own: until 1.99 the standard library
declared those three through a raw-dylib link attribute pointing at
api-ms-win-core-synch-l1-2-0, which makes the object carry its own import and needs no
import library; newer Rust declares them as ordinary imports, and then the linker has
to be told which library to take them from. The `__imp_` prefix in the message above is
exactly that "ordinary import" spelling.

Naming the library is the fix, and it is the fix upstream chose too: nodejs/node#67590
("build: add synchronization.lib to crates build on Windows", for issue nodejs/node#67589,
which is the same failure seen in Node's own Windows CI). That pull request was still
open when this patch was written, so the change is carried here and can be deleted once
the upstream one is released.

--- a/deps/crates/crates.gyp
+++ b/deps/crates/crates.gyp
@@ -81,6 +81,7 @@
           ['OS=="win"', {
             'libraries': [
               '-lntdll',
+              '-lsynchronization',
               '-luserenv'
             ],
           }],
